[ 2026-10-09 15:16:56,343 ] groq._base_client - DEBUG - Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/openai/v1/chat/completions', 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-063c76f0-8cb2-485c-a63e-c7901eaa46f9', 'json_data': {'messages': [{'role': 'system', 'content': "You are an expert Mechanical Engineering Assistant.\n\nProblem Categories: ['gear_design', 'shaft_design']\nTarget Operations: ['gear_ratio', 'output_speed', 'output_torque', 'power', 'shaft_diameter', 'shear_stress']\nExtracted Parameters: {'speed': 1200.0, 'power': 15.0, 'teeth_pinion': 20.0, 'teeth_gear': 60.0, 'efficiency': 100.0, 'bending_moment': 250.0, 'allowable_shear_stress': 50.0}\nAssociated Units: {'speed': 'RPM', 'power': 'kW', 'teeth_pinion': 'teeth', 'teeth_gear': 'teeth', 'efficiency': '%', 'bending_moment': 'N*m', 'allowable_shear_stress': 'MPa'}\n\nInstructions:\n1. Review the target operations and extracted parameters along with their specific units.\n2. Convert parameter units if needed before performing calculations.\n3. Invoke the necessary calculation/conversion tools using the exact numerical values and appropriate units.\n4. If multiple operations are required, execute all relevant tools in proper sequence.\n5. Do not invent or fabricate missing parameters.\n"}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Here is the clear, well-formatted statement for the engineering problem shown in your screenshot:\n\n---\n\n### **📝 Problem Statement: Gearbox & Shaft Design**\n\nA motor drives an input shaft carrying a spur gear at a speed of **$1200\\text{ RPM}$** with a power input of **$15\\text{ kW}$**. The motor pinion (**Gear A**) has **$20\\text{ teeth}$** and meshes with a driven gear (**Gear B**) having **$60\\text{ teeth}$** mounted on an output shaft.\n\nAssuming a mechanical efficiency of **$100\\%$**, perform the following calculations:\n\n#### **1. Gear Analysis:**\n\n* Calculate the gear ratio ($i$).\n\n\n* Calculate the output speed ($\\text{RPM}_{\\text{out}}$) of Gear B.\n\n\n* Calculate the output torque ($T_{\\text{out}}$) available at the output shaft in $\\text{N}\\cdot\\text{m}$.\n\n\n\n#### **2. Shaft Analysis:**\n\n* If the output shaft transmits this output torque ($T_{\\text{out}}$) and is subjected to an equivalent bending moment of $M = 250\\text{ N}\\cdot\\text{m}$, calculate the minimum required shaft diameter ($d$) using the von Mises shear stress criterion.\n\n\n\n#### **3. Material Specification:**\n\n* The shaft is made of steel with an allowable shear stress ($\\tau_{\\text{allow}}$) of **$50\\text{ MPa}$**.'}], 'model': 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 'n': 1, 'reasoning_effort': None, 'reasoning_format': None, 'service_tier': 'on_demand', 'stop': None, 'stream': False, 'temperature': 0.7, 'tools': [{'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'shaft_design', 'description': 'Design and analyze a solid circular shaft under torque and bending loads.\n\nSupported operations:\n\n1. shaft_diameter\n   Calculate required shaft diameter considering combined bending\n   and torsional loading.\n\n   Bending stress:\n       sigma = 32*M / (pi*d^3)\n\n   Torsional shear stress:\n       tau = 16*T / (pi*d^3)\n\n   Von Mises equivalent stress:\n       sigma_vm = sqrt(sigma^2 + 3*tau^2)\n\n   Required diameter:\n       d = [\n           (16 / (pi * allowable_stress))\n           * sqrt(4*M^2 + 3*T^2)\n       ]^(1/3)\n\n   Requires:\n       torque\n       bending_moment\n       allowable_stress\n\n2. torsional_stress\n   Calculate torsional shear stress in a solid circular shaft.\n\n       tau = 16*T / (pi*d^3)\n\n   Requires:\n       torque\n       diameter\n\n3. shear_stress\n   Calculate combined transverse and torsional shear stress.\n\n   Torsional shear:\n       tau_t = 16*T / (pi*d^3)\n\n   Average transverse shear:\n       tau_v = F / A\n\n   Conservative combined shear:\n       tau_total = tau_t + tau_v\n\n   Requires:\n       torque\n       diameter\n       transverse_force\n       area\n\n4. factor_of_safety\n   Calculate factor of safety using Von Mises stress.\n\n       sigma_b = 32*M / (pi*d^3)\n\n       tau_t = 16*T / (pi*d^3)\n\n       sigma_vm = sqrt(sigma_b^2 + 3*tau_t^2)\n\n       FoS = yield_strength / sigma_vm\n\n   Requires:\n       torque\n       bending_moment\n       diameter\n       yield_strength\n\nImportant:\n    All quantities must use a consistent unit system.\n\n    Example:\n        torque     -> N*m\n        bending    -> N*m\n        diameter   -> m\n        stress     -> Pa\n        yield      -> Pa\n\n    This implementation assumes a solid circular shaft.', 'parameters': {'properties': {'operation': {'enum': ['shaft_diameter', 'torsional_stress', 'shear_stress', 'factor_of_safety'], 'type': 'string'}, 'torque': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'bending_moment': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'diameter': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'allowable_stress': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'yield_strength': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'transverse_force': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'area': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}}, 'required': ['operation'], 'type': 'object'}}}, {'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'gear_design', 'description': 'Calculate gear ratio, output speed, output torque, or mechanical power.\n\nGear ratio:\n    GR = N_output / N_input\n\nFor an ideal gear pair:\n\n    n_output = n_input / GR\n\n    T_output = T_input * GR\n\nWith efficiency:\n\n    T_output = T_input * GR * efficiency\n\nMechanical power:\n\n    P = T * omega\n\nwhere:\n\n    omega = 2*pi*n / 60\n\nTherefore:\n\n    P = T * 2*pi*n / 60\n\nInputs:\n    input_speed:\n        Input shaft speed in RPM.\n\n    output_speed_value:\n        Output shaft speed in RPM.\n        Used when calculating gear ratio.\n\n    input_torque:\n        Input torque in N*m.\n\n    output_torque_value:\n        Output torque in N*m.\n        Used when calculating gear ratio from torque.\n\n    input_teeth:\n        Number of teeth on the driving/input gear.\n\n    output_teeth:\n        Number of teeth on the driven/output gear.\n\n    efficiency:\n        Gear transmission efficiency from 0 to 1.\n        Example:\n            0.95 = 95% efficiency.\n\nNotes:\n    - All speeds are RPM.\n    - Torque is N*m.\n    - Power is returned in Watts.\n    - For gear_ratio, teeth are preferred because they directly\n      determine the ratio.\n    - This tool assumes two externally meshing gears.', 'parameters': {'properties': {'operation': {'enum': ['gear_ratio', 'output_speed', 'output_torque', 'power'], 'type': 'string'}, 'input_speed': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'output_speed_value': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'input_torque': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'output_torque_value': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'input_teeth': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'integer'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'output_teeth': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'integer'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'efficiency': {'default': 1.0, 'type': 'number'}}, 'required': ['operation'], 'type': 'object'}}}, {'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'pump_power', 'description': 'Calculate pump hydraulic power, shaft power, and pump head.\n\n---------------------------------------------------------\n1. HYDRAULIC POWER\n---------------------------------------------------------\n\nHydraulic power:\n\n    P_h = Q * DeltaP\n\nwhere:\n\n    P_h = hydraulic power [W]\n    Q   = volumetric flow rate [m^3/s]\n    DeltaP = pressure increase [Pa]\n\nHydraulic power can also be calculated from head:\n\n    P_h = rho * g * Q * H\n\nwhere:\n\n    rho = fluid density [kg/m^3]\n    g   = gravitational acceleration [m/s^2]\n    H   = pump head [m]\n\n---------------------------------------------------------\n2. SHAFT POWER\n---------------------------------------------------------\n\nShaft power is the hydraulic power divided by pump efficiency:\n\n    P_shaft = P_h / eta\n\nTherefore:\n\n    P_shaft = Q * DeltaP / eta\n\nor:\n\n    P_shaft = rho * g * Q * H / eta\n\nwhere:\n\n    eta = pump efficiency\n\nEfficiency must be between 0 and 1.\n\n---------------------------------------------------------\n3. PUMP HEAD\n---------------------------------------------------------\n\nPump head from pressure difference:\n\n    H = DeltaP / (rho * g)\n\nwhere:\n\n    H = pump head [m]\n    DeltaP = pressure difference [Pa]\n    rho = fluid density [kg/m^3]\n    g = gravitational acceleration [m/s^2]\n\nUnits:\n\n    flow_rate        -> m^3/s\n    pressure_difference -> Pa\n    density          -> kg/m^3\n    head             -> m\n    efficiency       -> 0 to 1\n    hydraulic power  -> W\n    shaft power      -> W\n\nAssumptions:\n\n    - Steady-state operation\n    - Constant fluid density\n    - Pump efficiency is known\n    - Pressure_difference represents the pressure\n      increase produced by the pump', 'parameters': {'properties': {'operation': {'enum': ['hydraulic_power', 'shaft_power', 'pump_head'], 'type': 'string'}, 'flow_rate': {'type': 'number'}, 'pressure_difference': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'head': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'density': {'default': 1000.0, 'type': 'number'}, 'efficiency': {'default': 1.0, 'type': 'number'}, 'gravity': {'default': 9.81, 'type': 'number'}}, 'required': ['operation', 'flow_rate'], 'type': 'object'}}}]}}
